Exception: web2/src/core/digitnet_weights.json (handwritten-digit model weights)
is licensed under CC BY-SA 3.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/),
not MIT. The weights were trained by this repository (web2/tools/train_digitnet.py,
numpy only — no third-party model code) on the MNIST dataset (derived from NIST
Special Database 19). MNIST's own licensing is not stated by its original
distribution; several redistributors label it CC BY-SA 3.0, and this repository
conservatively assumes that label applies and complies with it (attribution:
Yann LeCun, Corinna Cortes, Christopher J.C. Burges, "THE MNIST DATABASE of
handwritten digits"). This notice is carried into deployed bundles via the
"license" field embedded in the weights JSON itself. The inference code
(web2/src/core/digitnet.ts) is MIT as above.

